---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { DIG, SUPPORT } from "../config/brand";
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Service — DIG for Discogs"
  description="Terms governing use of DIG for Discogs, an independent read-only service provided by WOIII.me."
  bodyClass="privacy-page"
  headerVariant="overlay"
>
  <section class="section privacy-section" data-header-tone="dark">
    <div class="wrap policy">
      <h1>Terms of <span class="accent">Service</span></h1>
      <p class="lede">
        These terms govern your use of DIG for Discogs, including its MCP
        server, REST API, browser extension, and supported AI-assistant
        integrations. DIG is provided by WOIII.me.
      </p>
      <p class="updated">Effective and last updated: 25 July 2026</p>

      <h2>Accepting these terms</h2>
      <p>
        By connecting to or using DIG, you agree to these terms and the{" "}
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy policy</a>. If you do not agree, do not use
        DIG and revoke or remove any existing connection. You must be legally
        able to accept these terms and meet the age requirements of Discogs,
        your AI provider, and other services you use with DIG.
      </p>

      <h2>What DIG provides</h2>
      <p>
        DIG is a read-only tool for searching and analyzing Discogs catalogue,
        collection, wantlist, community, and related permitted data. It can
        compare pressings, summarize a collection, and produce evidence-based
        recommendations. Features may change, be limited, or become unavailable.
      </p>

      <h2>Your accounts and authorization</h2>
      <p>
        You are responsible for the accounts and clients you connect, for
        keeping credentials secure, and for activity authorized through your
        connection. Do not share tokens or attempt to connect an account you do
        not control. You can revoke DIG from Discogs and remove it from your AI
        client at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You may not use DIG to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>access private or restricted data without authorization;</li>
        <li>bypass rate limits, access controls, or technical safeguards;</li>
        <li>scrape, bulk-export, resell, or build an unauthorized database from returned data;</li>
        <li>send malware, probe other users, interfere with the service, or expose credentials;</li>
        <li>violate applicable law or the terms and policies of Discogs, OpenAI, another AI provider, or another connected service.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Third-party services and content</h2>
      <p>
        DIG depends on Discogs, Cloudflare, your selected AI provider, and other
        software or network services. Their terms and privacy practices apply
        separately. Discogs data can be incomplete, user-contributed, delayed,
        or inaccurate. Marketplace values and availability can change at any
        time. Links and references do not imply an endorsement.
      </p>

      <h2>No purchases or professional advice</h2>
      <p>
        DIG does not buy or sell records, contact sellers, execute payments, or
        guarantee condition, authenticity, value, investment performance, or
        sound quality. Rankings and recommendations are informational estimates
        based on available evidence, not financial, appraisal, legal, or other
        professional advice. Verify important information before acting.
      </p>

      <h2>Open-source software</h2>
      <p>
        Source code made available through <a href={DIG.repoUrl}>the DIG repository</a>{" "}
        is licensed under the license stated in that repository. That software
        license does not replace these terms for the hosted service or grant
        rights in third-party data, names, or trademarks.
      </p>

      <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
      <p>
        DIG is provided on an “as available” basis. We may update, suspend,
        restrict, or discontinue features to protect users, comply with
        third-party requirements, maintain security, or operate the service.
        We may update these terms by publishing a revised version and date.
      </p>

      <h2>Disclaimers and liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the extent permitted by applicable law, DIG is provided without
        warranties of uninterrupted availability, accuracy, fitness for a
        particular purpose, or non-infringement. WOIII.me is not responsible for
        decisions, purchases, losses, or third-party actions based on DIG output.
        Nothing in these terms excludes rights or liability that cannot legally
        be excluded.
      </p>

      <h2>Suspension and termination</h2>
      <p>
        We may restrict or terminate access when reasonably necessary for
        security, abuse prevention, legal compliance, third-party requirements,
        or a material violation of these terms. You may stop using DIG at any
        time by revoking and removing its connections.
      </p>

      <h2>Discogs relationship</h2>
      <p>
        DIG for Discogs is an independent WOIII.me project. This application
        uses Discogs' API but is not affiliated with, sponsored or endorsed by
        Discogs. “Discogs” is a trademark of Zink Media, LLC.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT.email}`}>{SUPPORT.email}</a>.{" "}
        For product help, see <a href="/support">Support</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .privacy-section {
    --accent-hue: #c8ff9f;
    background: #000;
    padding-block: 170px 104px;
  }
  .privacy-section > .policy {
    --text-width: 62rem;
    width: min(100%, 1440px);
    max-width: 1440px;
    padding-inline: clamp(24px, 3.35vw, 48px);
  }
  .policy h2 {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    margin-top: calc(var(--space) * 7);
    margin-bottom: calc(var(--space) * 2.5);
    padding-top: calc(var(--space) * 4);
    max-width: var(--text-width);
  }
  .policy ul {
    padding-left: 1.1em;
    display: grid;
    gap: calc(var(--space) * 1.5);
    max-width: var(--text-width);
  }
  .policy li::marker {
    color: var(--ink-faint);
  }
  .policy p {
    margin-bottom: calc(var(--space) * 2);
  }
  .updated {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--ink-tertiary);
    margin-top: calc(var(--space) * 3);
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .privacy-section {
      padding-block: 125px 64px;
    }
  }
</style>
